WEBVTT

00:01.980 --> 00:11.860
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:02.350 --> 00:04.320
The Kalos League Miare Tournament is currently underway.

00:05.160 --> 00:08.650
Having advanced to the semifinals after a fierce fight,

00:09.110 --> 00:13.990
Satoshi settled on Numelgon as his sixth Pokémon, and will now face Shota with his best team!

00:15.050 --> 00:16.100
And finally,

00:16.810 --> 00:19.830
the time of their promised battle has come.

00:26.600 --> 00:27.290
Donnosuke!

00:31.500 --> 00:32.880
Dosidon is unable to battle!

00:33.620 --> 00:34.730
Lizardon wins!

00:35.440 --> 00:37.720
Louis' Dosidon has fallen as well!

00:38.210 --> 00:40.400
With that, five of Louis' Pokémon are down!

00:40.670 --> 00:42.860
He only has one left; his back is up against the wall now!

00:43.410 --> 00:44.280
Awesome!

00:45.790 --> 00:47.180
He's so strong!

00:47.340 --> 00:52.550
In all the battles he has had so far, Alan has only used two Pokémon; Metagross and Lizardon.

00:54.170 --> 00:56.670
It is still not possible to calculate his power.

00:57.100 --> 00:57.600
No.

01:00.150 --> 01:01.700
If we win this, we'll be in the finals.

01:02.540 --> 01:03.080
Lizardon!

01:03.530 --> 01:04.770
Brace yourself.

01:05.150 --> 01:05.610
All right?

01:09.430 --> 01:11.190
I'll strike everything down with this guy!

01:11.460 --> 01:13.130
Come on, Gabunoji!

01:19.420 --> 01:24.020
Ever since we lost to you guys, we've been going through some painful training.

01:24.960 --> 01:29.110
Day in and day out, the only thing we thought of was defeating you.

01:29.880 --> 01:34.090
I'll show you the results of our painstaking training!

01:36.580 --> 01:37.180
Gabunoji,

01:37.550 --> 01:39.780
let's go! Mega evolve!

01:46.370 --> 01:51.500
Whoa! Louis has now mega evolved Gablias! He's moving in for the kill!

01:52.420 --> 01:54.570
All right, watch this carefully.

01:54.760 --> 01:56.620
Gabunoji, Draco Meteor!

02:04.960 --> 02:05.530
Dodge!

02:11.570 --> 02:14.150
What do you think of Gabunoji's signature move?

02:14.860 --> 02:16.230
Respond to my heart,

02:16.650 --> 02:17.500
Key Stone!

02:18.020 --> 02:19.160
Surpass evolution!

02:19.680 --> 02:20.660
Mega evolve!

02:37.510 --> 02:41.920
Bless my heart! Now Alan's Lizardon has mega evolved too!

02:41.920 --> 02:44.600
This has turned into a clash between two Mega Evolutions!

02:44.860 --> 02:46.180
That's the spirit!

02:46.420 --> 02:48.420
Gabunoji, Dragon Rush!

02:51.110 --> 02:52.020
Dragon Claw!

02:56.080 --> 02:57.220
Lizardon, throw it!

03:00.110 --> 03:00.640
What?

03:00.820 --> 03:01.530
Flamethrower!

03:07.050 --> 03:08.040
Dragon Claw!

03:12.160 --> 03:12.790
Gabunoji!

03:15.720 --> 03:16.940
Gablias is unable to battle.

03:17.430 --> 03:19.550
Therefore, the winner is Alan!

03:20.320 --> 03:21.910
It's settled!

03:21.910 --> 03:24.830
The one who advances to the finals is Alan!

03:38.210 --> 03:39.450
Well done, Lizardon.

03:53.220 --> 03:58.890
Semifinal Full Battle!
Satoshi VS Shota!!

03:59.680 --> 04:01.260
It's finally time for my battle with Shota.

03:59.980 --> 04:09.860
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

03:59.980 --> 04:09.860
Z

04:04.490 --> 04:05.930
Until now, I've sometimes felt a little lost on what to do,

04:06.440 --> 04:07.220
come to a standstill,

04:07.750 --> 04:08.530
and been a burden, but...

04:09.570 --> 04:11.120
...thanks for believing in me despite everything.

04:12.650 --> 04:14.460
I believe in you guys!

04:19.440 --> 04:21.000
We're gonna win, guys! All right?

04:29.940 --> 04:30.810
It is time.

04:37.600 --> 04:40.890
I'm kinda nervous about the battle with Shota now.

04:41.880 --> 04:44.790
He lost to Shota once, right?

04:45.680 --> 04:47.320
Yes. He is not to be taken lightly.

04:48.090 --> 04:49.280
Now that I've battled him I realized something.

04:50.020 --> 04:51.370
His battle style is different,

04:52.010 --> 04:53.450
but still similar to Satoshi's.

04:54.540 --> 04:56.970
It's like... their auras, or something.

04:57.940 --> 04:59.550
Huh? Their auras are similar?

05:00.120 --> 05:03.200
Shota has been chasing after and analyzing Satoshi.

05:03.930 --> 05:06.580
That may be what you sensed, Tierno.

05:07.820 --> 05:13.660
A fight between Satoshi-kun, who battles with passion, and Shota-kun, who battles calmly and with an analytical mind...

05:14.410 --> 05:16.010
The two contrast each other, huh?

05:16.890 --> 05:19.560
I'm looking forward to how the battle will turn out.

05:20.400 --> 05:20.650
Me too.

05:22.320 --> 05:25.320
All right, this is the second match of the Kalos League semifinals.

05:25.940 --> 05:27.610
Both competitors are entering the stadium!

05:35.800 --> 05:37.120
Do your best, Satoshi!

05:37.560 --> 05:38.860
Do your best!

05:49.790 --> 05:51.550
First you need to capture their expressions!

05:52.470 --> 05:53.050
Okay!

05:53.510 --> 05:54.990
Ugh, I'm exhausted.

05:55.370 --> 05:57.740
Why do we need to film the brat boy?

05:58.270 --> 06:01.250
If anything, they should show <i>this beautiful face</i> on TV.

06:01.440 --> 06:03.610
Right, right. Not much longer now.

06:03.610 --> 06:05.700
We'll be done for today after this match.

06:05.960 --> 06:07.270
Geez!

06:10.170 --> 06:10.880
Satoshi.

06:11.670 --> 06:12.760
I will be waiting for you.

06:13.790 --> 06:14.200
Yeah.

06:16.810 --> 06:17.750
It is fine this way.

06:19.090 --> 06:20.490
The person I admire...

06:21.350 --> 06:22.600
...will definitely win.

06:24.630 --> 06:25.670
I want to surpass you.

06:26.800 --> 06:27.910
I want to defeat you...

06:28.560 --> 06:29.560
...and surpass you!

06:30.610 --> 06:31.060
Yeah.

06:31.770 --> 06:32.550
Bring it on!

06:33.330 --> 06:34.470
I won't lose this time.

06:38.140 --> 06:40.830
All right, today's battlefield is...

06:42.330 --> 06:44.110
...the forest field!

06:48.320 --> 06:52.430
The semifinal battle between Satoshi and Shota will now begin.

06:53.650 --> 06:55.020
You may use six Pokémon each.

06:55.670 --> 06:57.050
Pokémon may be substituted freely.

06:57.820 --> 07:00.490
As soon as one party's Pokémon are all unable to battle, the battle is over.

07:01.150 --> 07:08.310
Also, once three of either party's Pokémon are unable to battle, there will be an interval so we can change the battlefield.

07:11.290 --> 07:12.630
Both of you, please call out your Pokémon.

07:13.730 --> 07:15.450
Luchabull, I choose you!

07:32.950 --> 07:33.770
Luchabull?

07:34.410 --> 07:35.940
Hey, it looks kinda strange.

07:36.530 --> 07:37.250
You are right.

07:38.040 --> 07:39.850
Oh, the truth is, yesterday...

07:44.370 --> 07:45.640
Luchabull, what's the matter?

07:48.440 --> 07:48.780
Hm?

07:55.170 --> 07:56.450
I had no clue...

07:56.730 --> 08:01.000
Standing on this grand stage is a once-in-a-lifetime experience; when you win, you gotta be flashy and live up to your title of Forest Champion!

08:01.310 --> 08:01.800
Right!

08:02.540 --> 08:04.960
Luchabull, that looks great on you!

08:12.570 --> 08:14.640
So you have chosen Luchabull as your first.

08:15.380 --> 08:17.040
He's our assault trooper.

08:19.700 --> 08:20.650
Then I will use...

08:21.070 --> 08:22.070
...Kekking!

08:25.620 --> 08:26.930
Cute!

08:27.120 --> 08:27.850
Let's see...

08:29.870 --> 08:31.550
Kekking, the Lazy Pokémon.

08:32.320 --> 08:38.190
This Pokémon lives lying on its side. It only starts moving when there is no more grass to eat.

08:39.060 --> 08:40.410
I want to hug it!

08:40.690 --> 08:41.770
A Kekking, huh?

08:42.160 --> 08:45.560
Kekking has a type disadvantage against Luchabull.

08:46.270 --> 08:47.560
What kind of strategy is he going to use?

08:49.880 --> 08:50.430
Now then,

08:51.210 --> 08:52.380
begin the battle!

08:56.020 --> 08:58.550
Let's go, Luchabull! Let's make the first attack!

08:59.220 --> 09:00.340
Karate Chop!

09:10.720 --> 09:11.920
High Jump Kick!

09:20.090 --> 09:25.470
Whoa! In contrast to Luchabull, who's actively moving around, Kekking doesn't move at all!

09:25.840 --> 09:27.050
X-Scissor!

09:34.450 --> 09:39.690
Luchabull's battle style involves increasing its motivation as it takes hits from the opponent.

09:40.400 --> 09:42.120
If the opponent does not move at all...

09:42.420 --> 09:43.370
...fighting will be difficult.

09:43.620 --> 09:43.860
Yes.

09:44.660 --> 09:46.420
Attack it repeatedly, Satoshi!

09:46.810 --> 09:48.370
If it doesn't move, you can just push through!

09:48.830 --> 09:50.080
Luchabull, Karate Chop!

09:58.480 --> 10:00.810
Luchabull, keep using Karate Chop!

10:02.920 --> 10:06.940
Whoa, Luchabull's attacks are vicious! That must hurt even the likes of Kekking!

10:09.700 --> 10:11.390
Kekking has a triumphant look on its face!

10:11.840 --> 10:13.640
No, it's just bluffing!

10:14.050 --> 10:15.350
Huh? What do you mean?

10:15.910 --> 10:17.270
Kekking, Slack Off!

10:20.840 --> 10:21.730
Now?

10:22.510 --> 10:26.910
Slack Off is a move that makes the user regain health by relaxing.

10:27.350 --> 10:31.870
That said, if it keeps getting hit by attacks like this, it will lose eventually.

10:32.710 --> 10:34.870
What is Shota thinking?

10:43.670 --> 10:45.090
Here comes a Pokémon Quiz!

10:45.610 --> 10:46.460
The answer is...

10:47.930 --> 10:57.940
Coming up next:

10:47.930 --> 10:52.900
Shota's tactics are diverse!

10:48.820 --> 10:53.610
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

10:52.930 --> 10:57.940
How will Satoshi handle this tough fight!?

11:11.080 --> 11:12.140
This is Shota we're talking about.

11:12.810 --> 11:14.070
He's got to have something in mind.

11:15.040 --> 11:16.920
So we just need to defeat it before he does whatever he's planning!

11:17.730 --> 11:18.580
High Jump Kick!

11:22.860 --> 11:23.930
X-Scissor!

11:32.000 --> 11:33.130
Flying Press!

11:39.050 --> 11:40.110
Now, Kekking!

11:40.110 --> 11:41.100
Counter!

11:51.290 --> 11:52.120
Luchabull!

11:53.420 --> 11:54.480
Luchabull!

11:57.380 --> 11:58.330
Luchabull is unable to battle!

11:59.860 --> 12:01.050
Kekking wins!

12:01.640 --> 12:06.780
Luchabull was thought to have the upper hand in the battle, but it got knocked out with one hit!

12:08.570 --> 12:11.510
Luchabull, well done. Take a long rest.

12:12.550 --> 12:14.180
So that was your plan, Shota.

12:14.770 --> 12:17.330
I was thinking about using Kekking to counter Luchabull.

12:17.910 --> 12:23.100
After all, battling an opponent that does not move must be difficult for it.

12:24.070 --> 12:25.020
I've got to hand it to you.

12:25.520 --> 12:28.400
So you used Luchabull's battle style against it.

12:28.920 --> 12:30.640
I didn't know you could fight like that...

12:31.590 --> 12:35.160
Shota has planned out his strategy even better than I could imagine.

12:35.420 --> 12:38.230
All right, who will be Satoshi's second?

12:38.620 --> 12:40.380
Fiarrow, I choose you!

12:45.810 --> 12:46.810
Let's go, Fiarrow!

12:47.010 --> 12:48.090
Steel Wing!

12:53.910 --> 12:55.170
Kekking, Slack Off!

13:00.300 --> 13:02.560
Oh, it recovered again!

13:02.850 --> 13:05.900
He probably wants to drag the fight out and gun for a one-hit KO again.

13:06.400 --> 13:08.860
Luchabull's attacks are bound to have an effect at some point.

13:09.290 --> 13:11.070
Don't give it time to recover.

13:11.250 --> 13:13.100
Fiarrow, Flame Charge!

13:13.590 --> 13:17.520
Even using Slack Off will not let someone nullify the damage they have suffered.

13:18.050 --> 13:21.290
And that means the opponent will definitely get some exploitable weakness somewhere.

13:22.970 --> 13:24.050
Hammer Arm!

13:33.680 --> 13:35.190
Now, use Brave Bird!

13:42.640 --> 13:44.190
Kekking is unable to battle!

13:44.670 --> 13:45.830
Fiarrow wins!

13:46.420 --> 13:49.300
Fiarrow has claimed the victory with a furious attack!

13:50.300 --> 13:51.440
All right!

13:53.630 --> 13:55.220
Thank you for the hard work, Kekking.

13:55.850 --> 13:58.150
You have fulfilled your task sufficiently.

14:04.110 --> 14:06.390
All right, it is your turn next,

14:06.390 --> 14:07.300
Bloster!

14:11.310 --> 14:14.990
He is pitting Bloster, a Water type, against Fiarrow, a Fire type.

14:15.780 --> 14:17.010
He is going by the book.

14:17.950 --> 14:19.900
Bloster, Aqua Jet!

14:21.490 --> 14:22.250
Evade it!

14:23.600 --> 14:24.640
Is it following?

14:27.800 --> 14:30.270
I didn't know you could use Aqua Jet like that.

14:31.040 --> 14:32.650
He has an unconventional fighting style.

14:33.090 --> 14:33.430
Yeah,

14:34.010 --> 14:34.950
he's just like Satoshi.

14:35.630 --> 14:39.440
Our training was inspired by your way of thinking, Satoshi, and this is the result.

14:39.770 --> 14:40.460
You're good.

14:40.720 --> 14:41.870
Fiarrow, charge in!

14:42.170 --> 14:42.580
Now!

14:43.290 --> 14:44.590
Ice Beam!

14:46.480 --> 14:48.470
Burn it! Flame Charge!

14:56.700 --> 14:59.320
Nice one! It melted the ice with Flame Charge.

14:59.320 --> 15:00.150
Good job!

15:01.210 --> 15:02.140
Aqua Jet!

15:14.900 --> 15:15.630
Fiarrow!

15:17.820 --> 15:19.210
Fiarrow is unable to battle!

15:19.790 --> 15:20.930
Bloster wins!

15:21.650 --> 15:24.740
Incredibly, it is Bloster that has dominated in the mid-air fight!

15:27.340 --> 15:28.550
Thank you, Fiarrow.

15:29.220 --> 15:31.130
Speed is Fiarrow's characteristic trait,

15:31.710 --> 15:35.690
so I thought I had a chance of winning if I could stop its movements, if even for just one moment.

15:42.700 --> 15:45.820
Oh my, aren't things looking bad for the brat boy?

15:46.180 --> 15:47.420
He's under pressure.

15:47.420 --> 15:48.900
Don't tell me he's gonna lose...

15:49.730 --> 15:52.110
That'd feel bad in its own way.

15:52.770 --> 15:56.650
So far, it feels like things have been progressing as Shota planned.

15:57.140 --> 16:00.340
Shota really has studied Satoshi well.

16:01.100 --> 16:01.430
Yes.

16:02.780 --> 16:05.580
He has a complete grasp of Satoshi's data.

16:06.410 --> 16:07.930
He must have worked very hard.

16:10.170 --> 16:11.680
But Satoshi won't lose.

16:13.100 --> 16:15.810
Nobody can imitate Satoshi's current game.

16:20.020 --> 16:20.660
Next up is...

16:21.630 --> 16:23.390
Pikachu, I choose you!

16:25.460 --> 16:27.600
Satoshi's third is Pikachu!

16:28.960 --> 16:30.770
There you are, Pikachu.

16:31.270 --> 16:32.990
Do your best, Pikachu!

16:36.840 --> 16:38.030
I'm counting on you, Pikachu!

16:38.310 --> 16:39.710
Go into the forest and confuse it!

16:41.200 --> 16:42.890
Pikachu launched a preemptive strike!

16:43.290 --> 16:47.310
I can't believe how swift its movements are! This is what they call "faster than the eye can see"!

16:48.950 --> 16:50.250
Thunderbolt!

16:54.890 --> 16:55.340
Dodge!

16:56.850 --> 16:58.030
It dodged.

16:58.030 --> 16:58.920
It is not over yet!

16:59.290 --> 17:00.500
Quick Attack!

17:01.370 --> 17:02.300
Bloster, dodge!

17:07.110 --> 17:08.040
Ice Beam!

17:10.900 --> 17:11.270
Evade it!

17:13.100 --> 17:14.280
Electro Ball!

17:14.920 --> 17:16.520
Bloster, Dragon Pulse!

17:23.610 --> 17:26.080
Neither yields an inch in this incredibly close fight!

17:26.770 --> 17:30.730
If we defeat Pikachu now, we will have an overwhelming advantage.

17:31.130 --> 17:32.550
Bloster, let us go!

17:32.550 --> 17:34.080
Aqua Jet!

17:34.080 --> 17:34.900
Go into the forest!

17:41.050 --> 17:43.050
Now, use Iron Tail!

17:46.300 --> 17:46.970
Grab it with your pincer!

17:50.830 --> 17:52.410
Bloster has captured Pikachu!

17:53.320 --> 17:55.230
Bloster, now use Water Pulse!

17:57.510 --> 17:58.320
Electro Ball!

18:04.110 --> 18:05.260
Thunderbolt!

18:14.740 --> 18:15.460
Bloster!

18:17.740 --> 18:19.040
Bloster is unable to battle.

18:19.430 --> 18:20.670
Pikachu wins!

18:20.670 --> 18:21.670
All right!

18:22.330 --> 18:24.710
All right! Pikachu won!

18:25.610 --> 18:26.680
Now it's two against two!

18:27.290 --> 18:28.380
Marvelous.

18:29.030 --> 18:32.390
Satoshi-kun and his Pokémon really have an interesting fighting style.

18:33.290 --> 18:37.190
I can feel strong trust in both Trainer and Pokémon.

18:41.250 --> 18:42.770
Thank you for the hard work, Bloster.

18:45.220 --> 18:45.960
This is it.

18:46.480 --> 18:48.610
This is what battling Satoshi should be like.

18:50.650 --> 18:51.520
Welcome back,

18:52.310 --> 18:53.610
you who I admire.

18:55.600 --> 18:58.460
You really surprise me.

18:58.970 --> 19:01.120
Nah, that was a pretty close call.

19:01.450 --> 19:03.010
I wouldn't have been able to do it without Pikachu.

19:06.030 --> 19:08.220
All right, what Pokémon will you use next?

19:08.660 --> 19:10.870
Gillgard, please come out!

19:14.010 --> 19:16.940
Shota's third is Gillgard!

19:17.530 --> 19:18.490
Gillgard, huh...?

19:19.270 --> 19:21.440
How will he overcome King's Shield?

19:22.140 --> 19:23.110
Pikachu, let's go!

19:23.540 --> 19:24.870
Use the forest once more!

19:30.490 --> 19:33.080
Gillgard, Sacred Sword!

19:54.750 --> 19:55.630
What does this mean?

19:55.870 --> 19:56.730
I do not know.

19:57.230 --> 19:58.870
Nothing he does would surprise me.

19:59.490 --> 20:01.740
That is how seriously Shota is aiming for the victory.

20:02.380 --> 20:04.230
Please be careful, Satoshi.

20:08.100 --> 20:12.260
What will Satoshi and Shota's next moves be in their heated fight?

20:12.880 --> 20:15.210
How will the battle conclude?

20:16.290 --> 20:20.710
And who will advance to the finals?

20:26.330 --> 20:28.520
The passionate and exciting points of the Pokémon movie!

20:28.520 --> 20:29.610
Get blown away!

20:30.970 --> 21:21.050
The blockbuster is
currently in theaters!

20:31.130 --> 20:34.630
"Volcanion and the Ingenious Magearna" is a blockbuster currently in theaters.

20:35.300 --> 20:40.700
Apart from the obvious Volcanion and Magearna, who're the stars, Satoshi and his friends' Pokémon also play a big role!

20:41.050 --> 20:45.990
PIKACHU

20:41.480 --> 20:42.050
Pikachu,

20:46.060 --> 20:50.990
GEKKOUGA

20:47.280 --> 20:48.090
Gekkouga...

20:51.060 --> 21:01.000
SQUISHY

20:52.230 --> 20:52.800
...and Squishy!

20:56.140 --> 20:59.290
Finally, Squishy unleashes its true power!

21:01.370 --> 21:04.560
All of Serena's and Citron's Pokémon appear as well!

21:05.570 --> 21:09.100
A heartwarming story woven by cute Pokémon...

21:10.000 --> 21:13.210
...and spectacular battles that keep you on the edge of your seat.

21:14.020 --> 21:16.770
Root for your favorite Pokémon at the theater!

21:17.360 --> 21:19.900
This summer, get blown away to the theater!

21:21.050 --> 21:26.010
Sunday July 24th at 8am!

21:21.740 --> 21:22.920
Use Surf!

21:21.740 --> 21:24.180
Abareru-kun frolics around at a pool!

21:24.180 --> 21:25.610
On Sunday at 8am!

21:28.180 --> 21:30.090
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:30.290 --> 21:31.370
Towards our next adventure!

21:32.480 --> 21:34.770
Gillgard has King's Shield.

21:35.480 --> 21:37.440
If we don't break through it, we won't be able to defeat Shota.

21:38.880 --> 21:39.580
That's it...!

21:40.220 --> 21:42.090
That is the face he makes when he is about to start something...

21:42.580 --> 21:43.600
Let's go, Shota!

21:43.820 --> 21:45.130
Please bring it on!

21:45.130 --> 21:46.340
I accept your challenge!

21:46.530 --> 21:48.810
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:49.120 --> 21:52.330
Rival Showdown! Satoshi Gekkouga VS Mega Jukain!!

21:52.460 --> 21:55.910
Next Time

21:52.460 --> 21:55.910
Rival Showdown!
Satoshi Gekkouga VS Mega Jukain!!

21:52.830 --> 21:54.700
Everyone, get Pokémon!

21:55.940 --> 22:06.020
Next episode:

21:55.940 --> 22:00.950
Conclusion! Satoshi VS Shota!!

21:56.830 --> 22:01.350
Pocket Monsters XY&Z was brought to you by these sponsors.

22:00.950 --> 22:06.020
Who will advance to the finals against Alan!?
